## 1. Project Overview

A web-based point-of-sale app for a boarding school dorm store. Students log in with their school Gmail, browse available items, add them to a cart, and submit their purchase. Transactions are written directly to a Google Sheets workbook for analytics, P&L tracking, and daily reporting — with no third-party database involved.

Shopkeepers have an admin panel to manage items, prices, stock levels, and view reports.

---

## 2. Goals & Constraints

### Must-Have Features
- Google login (restricted to school domain)
- Student name and student number entry at checkout
- Item catalog with prices
- Cart and checkout flow
- Admin: add, edit, and remove items
- Admin: toggle items in/out of stock
- Out-of-stock items automatically greyed out
- Inventory tracking (stock received vs. sold)
- Export/log transactions to Google Sheets (per line item)
- Daily summary analytics (revenue, cost, profit per item)

### Constraints
- **No external databases** — all data lives in Google Sheets
- **No third-party student data storage** — only Google (which the school already uses)
- Hosted on **Vercel** (free tier to start)
- Must work well on **mobile** (students are on phones)

