## 4. System Architecture

```
Students / Shopkeeper
        │
        ▼
  Google OAuth  ──────────────────────────────────────┐
  (domain filter)                                      │
        │                                              │
        ▼                                              │
  Next.js App (Vercel)                                 │
  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐                  │
  │  Store UI  (item grid + cart)   │                  │
  │  Checkout  (student ID + items) │                  │
  │  Admin     (items, stock)       │                  │
  │  API routes (Sheets read/write) │                  │
  └──────────────┬──────────────────┘                  │
                 │                                     │
                 ▼                                     │
        Google Sheets API                              │
        (service account)                              │
                 │                                     │
                 ▼                                     │
        Google Sheets Workbook  ◄──────────────────────┘
        ┌─────────────┬──────────────┬─────────────┬──────────┐
        │   items     │ transactions │ stock_log   │  daily   │
        │             │              │             │ summary  │
        └─────────────┴──────────────┴─────────────┴──────────┘
```

**Key principle:** The Next.js app is stateless — it reads from and writes to Sheets on every relevant action. React state handles the cart client-side only; nothing is persisted until checkout is submitted.

