## 5. Google Sheets Structure

One shared workbook with four tabs.

### Tab 1: `items`

The source of truth for the item catalog.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | string | Unique item ID (e.g. `item_001`) |
| `name` | string | Display name |
| `category` | string | e.g. Snacks, Drinks, Hygiene |
| `price` | number | Sale price to student |
| `cost` | number | Cost to store (for P&L) |
| `stock_count` | number | Current on-hand quantity |
| `stock_received` | number | Running total units received (all time) |
| `stock_low_threshold` | number | Show "low stock" warning below this count |
| `in_stock` | boolean | Manual override (can force-disable regardless of count) |
| `active` | boolean | Soft delete — FALSE hides from catalog |

**Derived logic:** An item is purchasable only when `active = TRUE`, `in_stock = TRUE`, and `stock_count > 0`. If any condition fails, it is greyed out.

---

### Tab 2: `transactions`

One row per line item purchased. Each checkout creates multiple rows sharing a `transaction_id`.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `timestamp` | Full ISO datetime |
| `date` | Date only (for daily grouping) |
| `student_name` | Entered at checkout |
| `student_id` | Student number entered at checkout |
| `transaction_id` | Shared ID across all items in one checkout |
| `item_id` | Reference to `items.id` |
| `item_name` | Denormalised for readability |
| `qty` | Quantity purchased |
| `unit_price` | Price at time of purchase (snapshot) |
| `unit_cost` | Cost at time of purchase (snapshot) |
| `subtotal` | `qty × unit_price` |

---

### Tab 3: `stock_log`

Full audit trail of every stock movement — receipts and sales.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `timestamp` | Full ISO datetime |
| `item_id` | Reference to `items.id` |
| `item_name` | Denormalised |
| `type` | `received` or `sale` |
| `qty_change` | Positive (received) or negative (sale) |
| `new_total` | `stock_count` after this movement |
| `notes` | e.g. transaction ID for sales, delivery note for receipts |

**Shrinkage detection:** If `Σ stock_received − Σ sales ≠ current stock_count`, stock is unaccounted for.

---

### Tab 4: `daily_summary`

Appended each day (via cron or manual trigger).

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `date` | Date of summary |
| `total_revenue` | Sum of all subtotals |
| `total_cost` | Sum of all unit_cost × qty |
| `gross_profit` | `revenue − cost` |
| `transactions_count` | Number of checkouts |
| `top_item` | Best-selling item by revenue |
| `items_sold` | Total units sold |

Staff can build Sheets pivot tables and charts directly from this tab for P&L analysis.

